---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const updated = "October 28, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — GoodFat"
  description="How GoodFat handles food photos, your log, and your privacy."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 pb-24 pt-28 sm:px-8">
    <p class="label-micro text-yellow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-800 tracking-tight text-text">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      This policy explains what GoodFat does with your information. We wrote it in plain language so
      you can understand it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">1. The short version</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Meal photos stay on your iPhone.</strong> Apple Intelligence and
            Apple’s Vision framework read the photo on the device. GoodFat does not upload it and does
            not keep a photo library of your meals.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">We do not sell your data.</strong> We do not share your food log
            or profile with advertisers or data brokers.
          </li>
          <li>
            We use a few service partners only to run the account, the synced food log, and paywalls.
            Meal photos and questions are handled on the iPhone. Details are below.
          </li>
          <li>You can delete your account anytime in Settings.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">2. Who we are</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat (“we,” “us”) is the GoodFat mobile app and website at{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="https://goodfatbadfat.com"
            >goodfatbadfat.com</a
          >. Questions:{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="mailto:help@goodfatbadfat.com"
            >help@goodfatbadfat.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">3. Food photos (important)</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          When you take or pick a meal photo, GoodFat reads it on the iPhone. Apple’s Vision framework
          looks for a barcode or label text. Apple Intelligence names the food. Both run on the device.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text">We do not upload your food photos.</strong> We do not store them in
          your food log, and we do not keep a photo album on our servers. The photo is not sent to
          GoodFat or to a cloud model such as Google Gemini.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions you type in Ask are handled the same way: Apple Intelligence on the iPhone, then a
          lookup in the nutrition catalog stored on the phone. If the catalog is missing a fatty acid,
          GoodFat does not fill it in from a cloud model.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">4. What we collect</h2>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-800 text-text">Account</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              GoodFat can run with an anonymous account so you do not need an email to start. If you
              add a name or email in your profile, we store those fields with your account id.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-800 text-text">Food log</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              Foods you confirm (name, amount, nutrition fields, inflammatory score, and related
              details such as barcode or source). This is how your Today / Weekly / Monthly views
              work.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-800 text-text">Chat</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              Questions and replies in Ask stay on the iPhone. GoodFat does not send that conversation
              to a cloud model, and we do not keep a server log of those messages.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-800 text-text">On-device nutrition pack</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              A large US food catalog (sourced from public data such as USDA and Open Food Facts)
              lives on your phone. Lookups can happen without sending the whole catalog to us.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-base font-800 text-text">Subscriptions</h3>
            <p class="mt-1">
              If you subscribe, purchase status may be synced so Premium features unlock. See section
              6.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">5. How we use information</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>To identify foods and show nutrition and score estimates</li>
          <li>To keep your food log and trends</li>
          <li>To answer questions on your iPhone with Apple Intelligence</li>
          <li>To unlock paid features you buy</li>
          <li>To secure the service and fix bugs</li>
          <li>To respond if you contact support</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do <strong class="text-text">not</strong> use your food log to sell ads. We do{" "}
          <strong class="text-text">not</strong> sell personal information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">6. Sharing — and what we do not share</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-text"
            >We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties.</strong
          >
          We do not share your user profile or food log with other companies for their own marketing.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To run GoodFat we use a small set of processors that only get what they need to do their
          job:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Supabase</strong> — account auth, database, and secure edge
            functions
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Apple</strong> — Apple Intelligence and Vision run on your iPhone
            for meal photos and Ask. App Store billing applies when you buy Premium. Apple’s own terms
            cover on-device system features.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">RevenueCat</strong> — subscription status sync for Premium access
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may also share information if the law requires it, or to protect people from serious harm
          or fraud.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">7. Where data lives</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Meal photos and Ask stay on the iPhone. The nutrition pack is stored on the device. A copy of
          the food log also stays on the phone. If you have an account session, confirmed log entries
          (name, amount, nutrition fields, and score — not the photo) may sync to our cloud provider
          (Supabase).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">8. Keeping data</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Photos:</strong> processed on the iPhone and not uploaded to
            GoodFat.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Food log and account:</strong> kept on the phone, and in the
            cloud while your account exists.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Ask:</strong> stays on the iPhone. We do not keep a server copy of
            those messages.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">9. Your choices</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>You can use Ask without attaching a photo. Ask still runs on the iPhone.</li>
          <li>You can edit or remove foods from your log in the app.</li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Delete account</strong> in Settings removes your auth user and
            related cloud rows we control. Local copies on that phone are cleared when you delete the
            app.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          For privacy requests, email{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="mailto:help@goodfatbadfat.com"
            >help@goodfatbadfat.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">10. Children</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          GoodFat is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country). Do not
          use the app if you are under that age.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">11. Security</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We use standard industry protections (including encrypted connections). No method of
          storage or transfer is 100% safe, so please use a device you trust.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">12. Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If we update this policy, we will change the “Last updated” date on this page. Big changes
          may also be noted in the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">13. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Email{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="mailto:help@goodfatbadfat.com"
            >help@goodfatbadfat.com</a
          >. See also our{" "}
          <a class="text-yellow underline-offset-2 hover:underline" href="/terms">Terms of use</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">14. Website cookies and local storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The GoodFat website uses a small set of on-device preferences. These are not used to advertise
          to you.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Necessary:</strong> your light/dark theme choice and your cookie
            consent decision, stored in local storage on this device.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-text">Analytics (optional):</strong> if you tap “Accept analytics,” we
            may load privacy-minded measurement (Plausible and/or Google Analytics) to understand which
            pages are useful. This does not run until you accept.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can change your mind by clearing this site’s stored data in your browser. The banner
          will appear again if no consent choice is saved.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-800 text-text">15. Website contact form</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The support form checks the fields in your browser, then opens your email app with a draft to
          help@goodfatbadfat.com. The public website does not store that form. We receive the message
          only if you send the email. We do not use it to market to you.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
